    "body": "**Physical-iPhone Safari retest preview refreshed to exact PR #431 HEAD `af016d7ee57285ef3c87c1a2285b305354598c7a` (2026-10-31). Acceptance still pending.**\n\n- **UI-lab (start here)**: https://asynchronia-pr431-ui-lab.raykhalit.workers.dev/ . Provides separate chat, DM, report and profile/topbar test entrances without passing Stage 7.15. The lab uses preview-only overrides for Stage 7.15 and telemetry; the normal core, DM and CSS assets are fetched from exact PR SHA.\n- **Full-onboarding preview**: https://asynchronia-pr431-safari-preview.raykhalit.workers.dev/AsyncScene/ (retains Stage 7.15). \n- Both isolated Cloudflare Workers updated from `49847aa93a57f4ae262110586da9f43cb9590552` to `af016d7ee57285ef3c87c1a2285b305354598c7a`; no GitHub code modifications, merges, production or Chat03 staging changes.\n- Confirmed PR #431 **OPEN / DRAFT / UNMERGED**, eight scoped files; GitHub `ai-forensics-evidence` run [41142559516](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41142559516) SUCCESS. CI workflow is for forensics, **does not execute Chromium/DOM tests**. Codex reports browser **187/187 PASS** plus 10 fixture-only SKIP and Python **14/14 PASS**, but these were **not independently rerun here**.\n- Cloudflare Chromium independently checked **report lab at 320×568** and **DM lab at 390×844**: scenario ready, no lab errors. Assets `ui-core.js`, `ui-dm.js`, `style-base.css`, and overridden `telemetry-config.js` return HTTP 200 with `X-Preview-Commit: af016d7ee57285ef3c87c1a2285b305354598c7a`. Telemetry override confirmed disabled.\n- **Physical native Safari retest not yet performed for this SHA.** Owner to check compact profile bar while editing, empty and populated DM, journal vertical space, report dropdown positioning/artifact, keyboard focus and tab restore. No Safari PASS or merge approval implied. \n- Cleanup after acceptance: remove only preview Workers `asynchronia-pr431-ui-lab` and `asynchronia-pr431-safari-preview` from the Cloudflare account.\n\nScope: preview deployments only. PR #453 and `main` remain untouched.",
